      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The society’s second permanent home, completed recently, houses large historical artifacts and farming machinery beside its original building.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.harpersfieldhistoricalsociety.com/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Harpersfield’s northern edge borders Otsego County, and its western streams feed the Susquehanna River near Oneonta.",
